{"audio": "james-03.opus", "duration_ms": 137745, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 2120, "end_ms": 3380, "text": "James, Chapter Three."}, {"start_ms": 4580, "end_ms": 10580, "text": "Not many of you should become teachers, my brothers, because you know that we who teach will be judged more strictly."}, {"start_ms": 11240, "end_ms": 12700, "text": "We all stumble in many ways."}, {"start_ms": 13200, "end_ms": 18961, "text": "If anyone is never at fault in what he says, he is a perfect man, able to control his whole body."}, {"start_ms": 19861, "end_ms": 24901, "text": "When we put bits into the mouths of horses to make them obey us, we can guide the whole animal."}, {"start_ms": 25701, "end_ms": 26981, "text": "Consider ships as well."}, {"start_ms": 27321, "end_ms": 34381, "text": "Although they are so large and are driven by strong winds, they are steered by a very small rudder wherever the pilot is inclined."}, {"start_ms": 35361, "end_ms": 40041, "text": "In the same way, the tongue is a small part of the body, but it boasts of great things."}, {"start_ms": 40761, "end_ms": 44182, "text": "Consider how small a spark sets a great forest ablaze."}, {"start_ms": 44882, "end_ms": 49202, "text": "The tongue also is a fire, a world of wickedness among the parts of the body."}, {"start_ms": 49962, "end_ms": 56422, "text": "It pollutes the whole person, sets the course of his life on fire, and is itself set on fire by hell."}, {"start_ms": 57502, "end_ms": 66062, "text": "All kinds of animals, birds, reptiles, and creatures of the sea are being tamed and have been tamed by man, but no man can tame the tongue."}, {"start_ms": 66582, "end_ms": 69363, "text": "It is a restless evil, full of deadly poison."}, {"start_ms": 70243, "end_ms": 75903, "text": "With the tongue we bless our Lord and Father, and with it we curse men, who have been made in God’s likeness."}, {"start_ms": 76503, "end_ms": 79003, "text": "Out of the same mouth come blessing and cursing."}, {"start_ms": 79603, "end_ms": 81183, "text": "My brothers, this should not be!"}, {"start_ms": 81943, "end_ms": 85383, "text": "Can both fresh water and salt water flow from the same spring?"}, {"start_ms": 86063, "end_ms": 90283, "text": "My brothers, can a fig tree grow olives, or a grapevine bear figs?"}, {"start_ms": 90883, "end_ms": 93523, "text": "Neither can a salt spring produce fresh water."}, {"start_ms": 94483, "end_ms": 96744, "text": "Who is wise and understanding among you?"}, {"start_ms": 97124, "end_ms": 102164, "text": "Let him show it by his good conduct, by deeds done in the humility that comes from wisdom."}, {"start_ms": 102944, "end_ms": 109104, "text": "But if you harbor bitter jealousy and selfish ambition in your hearts, do not boast in it or deny the truth."}, {"start_ms": 109824, "end_ms": 115104, "text": "Such wisdom does not come from above, but is earthly, unspiritual, demonic."}, {"start_ms": 115844, "end_ms": 121224, "text": "For where jealousy and selfish ambition exist, there will be disorder and every evil practice."}, {"start_ms": 121884, "end_ms": 131465, "text": "But the wisdom from above is first of all pure, then peace-loving, gentle, accommodating, full of mercy and good fruit, impartial, and sincere."}, {"start_ms": 132365, "end_ms": 136305, "text": "Peacemakers who sow in peace reap the fruit of righteousness."}], "words": [{"t": "James,", "s": 2120, "e": 2580, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 2740, "e": 3080, "si": 0}, {"t": "Three.", "s": 3140, "e": 3380, "si": 0}, {"t": "Not", "s": 4580, "e": 4760, "si": 1}, {"t": "many", "s": 4840, "e": 5000, "si": 1}, {"t": "of", "s": 5060, "e": 5120, "si": 1}, {"t": "you", "s": 5180, "e": 5300, "si": 1}, {"t": "should", "s": 5380, "e": 5560, "si": 1}, {"t": "become", "s": 5580, "e": 5920, "si": 1}, {"t": "teachers,", "s": 6020, "e": 6540, "si": 1}, {"t": "my", "s": 6620, "e": 6740, "si": 1}, {"t": "brothers,", "s": 6780, "e": 7180, "si": 1}, {"t": "because", "s": 7300, "e": 7700, "si": 1}, {"t": "you", 